From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Gregoire <Benjamin.Gregoire@inria.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:26:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Safety conditions of the array and memory accesses

The conditions under which an array access succeeds are safety_cond terms
over the arguments [:: the array; the index; ...]: alignment
(sc_arr_aligned), bounds (sc_arr_in_bound) and initialisation
(sc_arr_init, an instance of sc_is_arr_init). sc_get, sc_set, sc_get_sub
and sc_set_sub list them in order with the error each one raises, checked
by check_safe_seq. For a memory access only the alignment of the pointer is
a condition on the arguments (sc_mem_aligned); its validity depends on the
memory.

getE, setE, get_subE and set_subE (safety_cond_facts.v) state that an
access in the partial mode succeeds exactly when its conditions hold and
then returns the value of the total mode. Each condition comes with its
evaluation lemma; WArray.validr_validw_init splits the readability of an
array range into validity and initialisation.

(cherry picked from commit 76707891048d32b7186bae40c35b957f86b398ae)
---
 proofs/lang/safety_cond.v       |  67 +++++++++++++++++++-
 proofs/lang/safety_cond_facts.v | 107 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 proofs/lang/warray_.v           |  10 +++
 3 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

